    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Observational oceanography",
    "problem": "Historically, shipboard ocean sampling has left vast expanses unobserved for long periods, creating spatial and seasonal data gaps that make it problematic to systematically monitor the ocean's crucial role in determining the planet's climate.",
    "method": "The paper describes the use of a global array of robotic profiling floats (the Argo array) to systematically sample the upper 2,000 m of the ocean, solving the problem of sparse, biased ship-based observations and enabling comprehensive, real-time monitoring of the ocean's role in the climate system.",
    "task": "The task is to review the progress and scientific contributions of the global Argo array over its first 15 years of observing the upper ocean, and to outline the program's future evolution and expansion.",
